meta {
  name: 01 Submit Feedback (pid1)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/feedback
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Cookie: copilot_session={{copilot_session}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "correlation_id": "fd899c3e-3101-44aa-a98e-6ac14d29f9ad",
    "rating": "up",
    "comment": "Correctly caught the duplicate record and flagged the odd AUDIT TEST problem-list entries.",
    "patient_id": "98c4b82b-b07e-11f1-8334-022958ad0af8"
  }
}

docs {
  Auth: requires the copilot_session environment variable to be set to a real,
  still-valid session cookie -- see bruno/README.md. Without it this 401s with
  {"detail": "Not logged in..."} regardless of the scenario below.

  correlation_id must be a real value from a `/chat` response's own
  `correlation_id` field, made under the SAME session this request uses --
  it is how the feedback gets attached to that turn's Langfuse trace
  (TurnObserver.attach_feedback_score re-derives the trace id by seeding
  create_trace_id with this value, it is never the trace id itself). The
  value saved here is real but historical (from chat/01's scenario, run
  live against the droplet 2026-09-20) -- it won't mean anything on a
  fresh run. Run chat/01 first, copy its response's correlation_id, and
  paste it in here before sending.

  rating is required ("up" or "down"); comment and patient_id are both
  optional. resident_username is never read from this body -- it always
  comes from the session, even if you add it here.

  Confirmed live 2026-09-20 against the droplet, with a real correlation_id
  from a real chat/01 call under this same session: 200
    {"status": "recorded", "langfuse_attached": true}
  -- and independently confirmed both durable copies actually landed: the
  entry appended to feedback.jsonl, and a `resident_feedback` score (value
  1, this exact comment) on the turn's real Langfuse trace, found by
  querying the droplet's ClickHouse directly for the same trace_id
  TurnObserver derives from this correlation_id.
}
